 102: Q2: WHICH ACCEPTED DISPOSITION IS WRONG? -- F4 / D7.
 103: ================================================================================
 104: 
 105: Of the coordinator's 21 accepted-or-refined dispositions, the wrong one is **F4 (and its disagreement-ruling D7)**: D2_and_st was graded "EQUIVALENT ON GUEST CHANNELS, disclosed; no row," and it is a FLOOR cell with a measured guest INTRQ delta. The coordinator's own section-4 self-doubt pointed here ("agreement is not evidence"; the packet even posed it as question 2), and the discriminator the coordinator applied correctly elsewhere -- *is the swapped operand a repair-path lvalue?* -- answers YES for atapi_st (F4) and NO for the latches (F10/F11/F18/F19). The coordinator described F4 by the field that co-varies (warned_null_xfer, a latch) instead of by the operand that was swapped (atapi_st, a repair-path lvalue), and that framing produced the wrong grade. It is a one-row cost and, because REPAIR4 is pre-ship, L1 construction -- but left unfixed it is a clean-sweep escape the closing pass would find (the #499 pattern: the symmetric half of a joint left open).
 106: 
 107: No other accepted disposition is wrong on my check. The 20 EQUIVALENT/(e)/OUT/RECORD grades each rest on a fact I either read (the result domain {0,1,2}, the phase/flag co-writers, the width reachability, the drain's write_in_progress gate, status_byte's 0x50) or measured (the D2_phase/D3_ge0/D7_lt1/D8_lt2 controls came back matching HEAD in the same harness run).
 108: 
 109: ================================================================================
 110: Q3: WHAT DID ALL OF US MISS?
 111: ================================================================================
 112: 
 113: **The class is NAMED correctly** ("the operand-swap axis of every dominating guard"). **The ENUMERATION is incomplete by one floor cell, and S4's G0-G13 + S4A's additions mis-graded it.** S4 1's G3 bullet enumerated the (flag x atapi_st) joint and wrote the (flag 1, st NULL) cell as "guest-EQUIVALENT ... only warned_null_xfer differs." That is the cell I measured as a guest INTRQ escape. So the missing member is:
 114: 
 115: > **(flag 1, atapi_st NULL, phase CMDOUT, ring occupancy a nonzero multiple of 512 after the read's pops)** -- reached by: ATAPI_PKT_CMD, then data-port writes stepping occupancy 2,6,10,14 (one 2-byte then three 4-byte stores) and 2-byte stores on to 514, then one width-2 DATA read. HEAD latches warned_null_xfer and asserts nothing; D2_and_st (and D2_st) take the PIO arm and assert INTRQ. MEASURED, fable5/meas_A/f4_run.txt.
 116: 
 117: S4A came CLOSEST -- it built the 514-byte boundary read -- but applied it to the `warned_null_xfer` operand (correctly (e)) and never to the `atapi_st` operand (which is floor). The coordinator, FR (mine), minimax and the ruling all treated the (flag 1, st NULL) cell as latch-only. The complete (flag x atapi_st) floor joint has FOUR cells: (0,NULL) HEAD-equal; (0,non-NULL) Row 1/Row 2 [N1/N2]; (1,NULL) **N5 [missing]**; (1,non-NULL) the existing re-arm rows. REPAIR4 must close all four in one diff.
 118: 
 119: ================================================================================
 120: Q4: IS REPAIR4 (N1-N4 + R14/R15 + contract) SUFFICIENT FOR THE CLOSING PASS?
 121: ================================================================================
 122: 
 123: **No.** As drafted it closes only the flag-0 half of the (flag x atapi_st) joint, so the closing pass re-measuring the enumeration would find D2_and_st escaping 159/159 -- the exact repair-chain failure mode (a symmetric cell left open). The smallest change that makes it sufficient:
 124: 
 125: 1. **Add row N5** `CMDOUT boundary read, no transfer` (name <= 36 chars): fixture = enter CMDOUT (flag 1, phase CMDOUT, st NULL, atapi_len 0), push occupancy to 514 through real data-port stores stepping past 12 (2,6,10,14,... as above), one width-2 DATA read; ORACLE `rep_asserts == 0 && warned_null_xfer == 1` (HEAD's behaviour). It reddens D2_and_st AND D2_st on this cell (both take PIO and assert; both set warned_null_xfer 0). It cannot redden an unchanged row: no existing fixture builds occ-514-CMDOUT, and D2_or_st/D2_phase/the equivalents stay on HEAD's ATAPI arm here. CHANNEL: INTRQ (and the latch), knowable at writing time. Measured basis: fable5/meas_A/f4_run.txt.
 126: 2. **Write the full (flag x atapi_st) cross-product into the contract**: four cells, which rows cover which (N1/N2 the flag-0 pair; N5 the (1,NULL) cell; the re-arm rows the (1,non-NULL) cell), so the closing pass VERIFIES the enumeration rather than hunts cells -- the class-closure amendment's own requirement.
 127: 3. **N1-N4 otherwise stand** (D6: S4's two rows over FR's one-line edit; N3 for F20; N4 for VD1). R14/R15 oracle additions stand.
 128: 4. The PRETABLE for REPAIR4 must MEASURE N5 on HEAD, D2_st, D2_or_st, D2_and_st and D2_phase before table 1 (F25), since N5 is precisely the row the un-run scratch-row stage would have forced.
 129: 
 130: With N5 added, the closing pass can report a VALID zero (diff delivered, roster stated, the enumeration named with its denominator) and the chain closes -- provided that pass finds zero further breaches of the class.
