C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/fable5/fable5_adj_A_563_v2.md:45:Grade: VD1 is floor; cons_eq2, bepop_ge4 and lepop_ge4 are disclosed debt. The width `len` is an input the handler tests directly at :1255 (`len == 4`, `len >= 2`) and at the pop sites; the 2026-10-09 derived-input ruling attaches to the computed local `consumed`, not to those tests, so it does not make the width cells all debt. The tests separate three cases: {1}, {2,3,5,6,7,8}, {4}. VD1 changes only the width-1 case, whose sole row cannot see the change -- floor, one count read fixes it. cons_eq2 and the pops change behaviour only at widths 3 and 5-8, inside the bucket the handler does not split from width 2 -- debt, written down with the width-8 delta.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/fable5/fable5_adj_A_563_v2.md:51:Yes: it is a coverage row the next repair owes. The dispatch fires only at occupancy exactly 12 (:1717), and a run of stores can step over it (2, 6, 10, 14, then 2-byte stores to 514) without ever dispatching -- f4_run.txt confirms `st=NULL phase=0x9 dispatched=no` at occupancy 514 with every store driven through the real handler. One width-2 read then pops two bytes before the flag test (occupancy 512), and the PIO branch's 512-boundary test fires. HEAD, with the flag set, takes the transfer-accounting branch, latches warned_null_xfer and raises no interrupt; D2_and_st, finding atapi_st NULL, takes the PIO branch and raises one (`sink=1`). The operand it swaps in, atapi_st, is read by the repaired refill (:1424, :1461), so (flag x atapi_st) is a floor joint -- the coordinator already grades its (flag 0, non-NULL) cells floor (Rows 1 and 2) -- and this is its (flag 1, NULL) cell. No existing row builds that occupancy (the one flag-1/NULL row reads an empty ring and checks only that the process did not terminate), which is why the variant went undetected 159/159. Row N5: enter CMDOUT, drive occupancy to 514 through data-port stores, one width-2 read, want no interrupt and the latch set. It detects D2_and_st and D2_st on this cell; D2_or_st, D2_phase and the equivalents match HEAD here (f4_run.txt), so it cannot redden an unchanged row. Without it the next repair closes half a joint and the pass after finds the other half -- the pattern the repair-chain rule exists to stop.
