C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/fable5/FALLBACK_opus48_adj_A_563.md:39:**Grade: FLOOR.** The read-arm flag guard (:1228) dominates the re-arm repair (clamp :1427, refill :1460). The repair path reads `d->atapi_st` (:1424 `d->atapi_st->data_in_len`, :1461 `d->atapi_st->data_in[...]`), so `atapi_st` is a repair-path lvalue and (flag x atapi_st) is in pass-11's floor cross-product -- the SAME joint that makes D2_st and D2_or_st FLOOR (coordinator agrees for those). D2_and_st pins the (flag 1, st NULL) cell of that joint; it is reachable (measured) and guest-distinguishable (measured). FLOOR. The 159-row table scores it 0/159 (SCORES.txt), i.e. it ESCAPES; no existing row builds the occ-514-CMDOUT state (the only (flag 1, st NULL) row, `row_null_atapi_st`, does one read on an EMPTY ring in DATAIN and forks checking only WIFSIGNALED). This is exactly the #499 shape the repair-chain amendment warns of: the coordinator's N1/N2 close the (flag 0, *) half of the joint and leave the (flag 1, NULL) half open for the next pass.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/fable5/FALLBACK_opus48_adj_A_563.md:59:- **cons_eq2 and bepop_ge4/lepop_ge4 -> (e) DISCLOSED.** cons_eq2 (`len >= 2` -> `len == 2`) and the pops (`len == 4` -> `len >= 4`) differ ONLY at widths {3,5,6,7,8}. Widths 3,5,6,7 are unreachable; width 8 is reachable but BUCKETED with width 2 (not a case the body distinguishes from 2), so it is a value inside the `{2,3,5,6,7,8}` bucket -- clause-(e) coverage debt with a named width-8 delta, exactly as the contract already discloses for `n_C6`/`n_E_cons_ge4`. The far (past-bound) region of `len >= 2` has its BRANCH discharged by the width-2 rows; a width-8 row would only pin the branch, and there is no further bound to pin. So no floor row is owed.
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/fable5/FALLBACK_opus48_adj_A_563.md:61:The coordinator wrote it was "least sure of this ruling of any." It is sound: the derived-input ruling attaches to `consumed`, not to `len`; width 1 is a genuine below-bound/case cell with a blind row (floor); the width-8 delta is real (reachable) but bucketed (disclosed). One OPTIONAL width-8 read row would collapse cons_eq2, both pops, n_C6 and n_E_cons_ge4 at once (GA, kimi substitute) -- worth noting as cheap coverage, but NOT floor-owed.
