C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/fable5/FALLBACK_opus48_adj_A_563.md:105:Of the coordinator's 21 accepted-or-refined dispositions, the wrong one is **F4 (and its disagreement-ruling D7)**: D2_and_st was graded "EQUIVALENT ON GUEST CHANNELS, disclosed; no row," and it is a FLOOR cell with a measured guest INTRQ delta. The coordinator's own section-4 self-doubt pointed here ("agreement is not evidence"; the packet even posed it as question 2), and the discriminator the coordinator applied correctly elsewhere -- *is the swapped operand a repair-path lvalue?* -- answers YES for atapi_st (F4) and NO for the latches (F10/F11/F18/F19). The coordinator described F4 by the field that co-varies (warned_null_xfer, a latch) instead of by the operand that was swapped (atapi_st, a repair-path lvalue), and that framing produced the wrong grade. It is a one-row cost and, because REPAIR4 is pre-ship, L1 construction -- but left unfixed it is a clean-sweep escape the closing pass would find (the #499 pattern: the symmetric half of a joint left open).
C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/fable5/FALLBACK_opus48_adj_A_563.md:117:S4A came CLOSEST -- it built the 514-byte boundary read -- but applied it to the `warned_null_xfer` operand (correctly (e)) and never to the `atapi_st` operand (which is floor). The coordinator, FR (mine), minimax and the ruling all treated the (flag 1, st NULL) cell as latch-only. The complete (flag x atapi_st) floor joint has FOUR cells: (0,NULL) HEAD-equal; (0,non-NULL) Row 1/Row 2 [N1/N2]; (1,NULL) **N5 [missing]**; (1,non-NULL) the existing re-arm rows. REPAIR4 must close all four in one diff.
