VERDICT: 5 flags -- A13 is wrongly confirmed; A3’s wording attribution and three block details need correction.

Q1.

Paths below are relative to `GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/`.

FLAG: A3: PARTLY -- Fable supports the insufficiency conclusion (`fable5/fable5_adj_A_563_v2.md:51`). But “the chain does NOT close” is the main loop’s paraphrase (`RULINGS_A_563.md:11`), not FB-A’s or Astra’s wording; their conclusions appear at `fable5/FALLBACK_opus48_adj_A_563.md:9,123` and `astra/A_563/codex_adjA.txt:115,117`. Attribute the paraphrase accordingly.

A5: RIGHT -- Grok supplies both the refuted channel premise and the latch classification; preserving both accurately clarifies its reasoning (`grok/A_563/grok_adjA.txt:13,41,59`).

A11: RIGHT -- The numerical witness is Grok’s and the packet’s; Astra independently identifies lost wrapped dispatch (`grok/A_563/grok_adjA.txt:47`; `packet_A_563.md:140`; `astra/A_563/codex_adjA.txt:60,62`).

A12: RIGHT -- “3/3” overstates agreement: Grok explicitly cannot settle the numerical records, and Astra requires refinements (`grok/A_563/grok_adjA.txt:26`; `astra/A_563/codex_adjA.txt:25`).

FLAG: A13: WRONG -- The original explicitly says “extended,” without claiming unanimity (`RULINGS_A_563.md:68`). Astra prescribed the additional G0/G2 cells, N5 and width fixture (`astra/A_563/codex_adjA.txt:33,119,120,121,141`). The accurate provenance is “the main loop adopted Astra’s extension over Grok’s dissent.” Recording that dissent is useful; the enlarged PRETABLE was already supported.

A14: RIGHT -- N2’s one-sided qualification and N3’s separately driven reachability measurement were genuinely omitted (`astra/A_563/codex_adjA.txt:135,141`). Width coverage already existed (`RULINGS_A_563.md:66,108`).

B1: RIGHT -- As a clarification: the original already distinguishes rewriting Record 3 from making the existing comment true through pin C (`RULINGS_B_asic.md:24`; `fable5/fable5_adj_B_asic.md:35,44,116`).

B2: RIGHT -- The absence objection overlooks chronology, while the two CPU issues require separation (`fidelity_20261018/fid_brief.md:29`; `fable5/fable5_adj_B_asic.md:47`; `prescreen/prescreen_asic.md:291`).

B6: RIGHT -- The contrary upholds were omitted; the adopted scope interpretation is Astra’s (`grok/B_asic/grok_adjB.txt:36`; `fable5/fable5_adj_B_asic.md:55`; `astra/B_asic/codex_adjB.txt:36`).

B9: RIGHT -- The ruling omitted provenance for its later prescreen reading; all three seats reported the file absent (`RULINGS_B_asic.md:73`; `astra/B_asic/codex_adjB.txt:117`; `grok/B_asic/grok_adjB.txt:63`; `fable5/fable5_adj_B_asic.md:15`).

B10: RIGHT -- Grok’s explicit successful-link/runtime distinction and Record 1 instruction were omitted (`grok/B_asic/grok_adjB.txt:34,40`; `RULINGS_B_asic.md:51`). Block B3 nevertheless needs the correction below.

B11: RIGHT -- “Made explicit” correctly acknowledges prior incorporation through Fable §7 (`RULINGS_B_asic.md:80`; `fable5/fable5_adj_B_asic.md:45,116`).

B12: RIGHT -- The LeakSanitizer disclosure and gate VOID sentence were likewise already incorporated (`RULINGS_B_asic.md:80`; `fable5/fable5_adj_B_asic.md:57,116`).

Q2.

FLAG: Block A7’s address count is wrong. “Four WDC addresses” lists **five addresses in four groups**: `0x1f0`, `0x170`, `0x900001f0`, `0x14000180`, `0x14000000`. Correct the count or say “four groups” (`fidelity_20261018/packet_fidf2_ASTRA.md:84`; `fable5/fable5_adj_A_563_v2.md:47`).

FLAG: Block B2 falsely calls `SYSASIC_EVENT_TO_ADDR(e) * 2` an **in-tree use**. Fable says the removals are equivalent for every in-tree use and supplies that expression as a hypothetical exposing context. Delete “in-tree” (`fidelity_20261018/packet_fidf2_ASTRA.md:106`; `fable5/fable5_adj_B_asic.md:45`).

FLAG: Block B3 misidentifies the code distinction and states VOID too broadly. `id_verdict` tests compile/link `rc` separately from `run_rc`; candidate compilation failures remain row FAIL. The independent capability preflight produces VOID on compile, link **or startup** failure. Preserve those boundaries, including missing-field RED BY DESIGN (`fidelity_20261018/packet_fidf2_ASTRA.md:109`; `fable5/meas_B/variants/pinned_preflight/sysasic_range_check.py:414,434,675`; `fable5/fable5_adj_B_asic.md:47,57`).

The A3 and A13 defects above also affect block A’s attribution text. Block B6’s external DeepSeek original was outside the permitted reading scope; its account is supported indirectly by `astra/B_asic/codex_adjB.txt:19,34`.

Q3.

No additional definite build-changing omission established beyond B3. The general per-guard ledger must still discharge all applicable enabled/direction partitions, including enabled WRITE counterparts (`RULINGS_A_563.md:89`; `astra/A_563/codex_adjA.txt:99,120`).
